# Cursor Rules -- Acme Dashboard (Next.js pnpm Monorepo)

Read CLAUDE.md before starting any task. It contains project architecture,
commands, and conventions that must be followed.

## Project Structure

This is a pnpm monorepo managed by Turborepo:
- `apps/web` -- Next.js 14 App Router (customer-facing dashboard)
- `apps/api` -- Next.js Pages Router (REST API at /api/v1/*)
- `packages/database` -- Drizzle ORM schemas, migrations, repositories
- `packages/shared` -- Zod schemas, TypeScript types, shared constants

## General Rules

- Use TypeScript strict mode. No `any` types unless explicitly justified with a comment.
- Use named exports everywhere. Default exports only for Next.js pages, layouts, and route handlers.
- Import from workspace packages using `@acme/database` or `@acme/shared`, never relative paths across package boundaries.
- Colocate test files next to the code they test: `Widget.tsx` -> `Widget.test.tsx`.
- Keep files under 300 lines. Extract logic into hooks, utilities, or sub-components.
- Use `satisfies` for type-safe object literals instead of type annotations where possible.

## TypeScript Conventions

- Prefer `interface` for object shapes that may be extended. Use `type` for unions, intersections, and mapped types.
- Use Zod schemas from `@acme/shared` as the source of truth. Derive TypeScript types with `z.infer<typeof schema>`.
- Avoid enums. Use `as const` objects with a union type derived from values.
- Function parameters: use destructured objects for 3+ parameters.

## React / Next.js Conventions

- Components are server components by default. Only add `"use client"` when the component needs browser APIs, event handlers, or React state.
- Use the App Router patterns: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`.
- Data fetching happens in server components or route handlers, never in client components directly.
- Use `next/image` for all images. Never use raw `<img>` tags.
- Use `next/link` for internal navigation. Never use raw `<a>` tags for internal links.
- Forms: use React Hook Form with Zod resolvers from `@acme/shared`.

## Component Patterns

- Use function declarations for components: `function Widget({ title }: WidgetProps) {`
- Props interface named `[ComponentName]Props` and defined directly above the component.
- Avoid prop drilling beyond 2 levels. Use React Context or composition patterns.
- UI primitives come from shadcn/ui (`@/components/ui/*`). Do not install additional UI libraries.
- Custom components go in `@/components/` organized by feature, not by type.

## Styling

- Tailwind CSS only. No CSS modules, styled-components, or inline styles.
- Use `cn()` utility from `@/lib/utils` for conditional class names (clsx + twMerge).
- Design tokens come from `tailwind.config.ts`. Use semantic color names (e.g., `text-primary`, `bg-destructive`), not raw colors.
- Responsive: mobile-first. Use `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` breakpoints.

## API Routes (apps/api)

- All API routes live under `pages/api/v1/`.
- Use the handler pattern: export default wrapped with `withErrorHandler()`.
- Validate request bodies with Zod schemas: `const body = RequestSchema.parse(req.body)`.
- Response format: `{ data: T, error: null }` on success, `{ data: null, error: { message, code } }` on failure.
- Authentication: use `withAuth()` middleware. Access user via `req.user`.
- Rate limiting configured per-route via `withRateLimit()`.

## Database (packages/database)

- Schema files: one file per domain entity in `src/schema/`.
- Naming: tables use `snake_case`, TypeScript fields use `camelCase` (Drizzle handles mapping).
- All queries go through repository classes in `src/repositories/`.
- Repositories accept a `db` parameter for testability. Never import a global db instance inside a repository.
- Migrations: never edit existing migration files. Always generate a new migration.
- Use transactions for multi-table writes: `db.transaction(async (tx) => { ... })`.

## Testing

- Unit tests: Vitest. Test business logic and utilities. Mock external dependencies.
- Component tests: Vitest + Testing Library. Test behavior, not implementation.
- E2E tests: Playwright in `tests/e2e/`. Test critical user flows.
- Test file naming: `*.test.ts` for unit, `*.spec.ts` for E2E.
- Use `describe`/`it` blocks. Test names should read as sentences: `it("returns 401 when token is expired")`.
- Fixtures and factories in `tests/fixtures/`. Use `createTestUser()` style helpers.

## Git Workflow

- Branch from `development`. Never commit directly to `main` or `development`.
- Branch naming: `feat/PROJ-123-short-description` or `fix/PROJ-456-short-description`.
- Commit messages: conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `test:`, `docs:`).
- PR titles: `type(scope): description (PROJ-123)`.
- Keep PRs focused. One logical change per PR. Under 400 lines of diff when possible.

## Security

- Never log or expose secrets, tokens, or passwords.
- Sanitize user input before database queries (Drizzle parameterizes by default).
- Validate all external input at API boundaries with Zod.
- Use `httpOnly` and `secure` flags on cookies.
- CSP headers configured in `next.config.js`.

## Performance

- Use React `Suspense` boundaries with meaningful loading states.
- Lazy load heavy client components with `next/dynamic`.
- Database queries: always add `.limit()` to list queries. Index columns used in `WHERE` clauses.
- Use Turborepo remote caching in CI. Local caching enabled by default.

## Error Handling

- API: use `AppError` class from `apps/api/src/lib/errors.ts` with appropriate HTTP status codes.
- Client: use error boundaries (`error.tsx`) per route segment.
- Log errors with structured fields via `pino`. Include request ID for tracing.
- Never show raw error messages to users in production.

## Accessibility

- All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible.
- Use semantic HTML elements (`button`, `nav`, `main`, `section`).
- Images require meaningful `alt` text. Decorative images use `alt=""`.
- Use `aria-label` on icon-only buttons.
- Color is never the sole indicator of state -- always add icons or text.

## Import Order

Imports should follow this order, separated by blank lines:
1. React / Next.js imports
2. Third-party library imports
3. Workspace package imports (`@acme/*`)
4. Local imports (`@/`, `./`)
5. Type-only imports (`import type { ... }`)

ESLint enforces this via `eslint-plugin-import` with the project configuration.
